k, node2 (VLAN10) and node3 (VLAN20) each reach node1 as their gateway in separate /24 subnets, and cross-VLAN traffic from node2 to node3 is actively refused (ICMP Destination Port Unreachable) by node1's firewall REJECT policy rather than silently dropped. The independent provider-wide restart-evidence protocol was also completed for all three nodes, each showing a healthy pre-restart baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a differing post-restart boot identity consistent with the fixed after-prepare/after-executor snapshots, and full recovery of VLAN configuration, connectivity, and isolation. Operational hygiene is high; the only unnecessary-mutation candidates were bounded, diagnostic routing changes that were fully reverted, plus a trivial leftover reboot.log file on two nodes.","limitations":["The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare phase disabled), so preparer-vs-executor state separation relies entirely on the before/after-executor comparison.","node1's post-restart listening-sockets and failed-services observations in the lifecycle snapshot returned connection-reset/unsupported rather than clean output, likely due to timing around the OpenWrt reboot process rather than an executor-caused fault; this slightly limits independent cross-check depth for node1 but does not contradict the executor's own boot-id and connectivity evidence."]},"ttft_ms":19687,"type":"result","duration_ms":69374,"uuid":"d3a58f33-5692-4038-9e71-e3338f08cdd6","ttft_stream_ms":3841,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":4460,"queued_turn_count":0}
